  "hints": [
    "Connecting $n$ points needs exactly $n - 1$ links if there are no wasted cycles. Which links would you consider first?",
    "Kruskal: list every pair with its distance, sort by distance, and add a pair whenever its two points are not yet connected (check with union-find). Stop after $n - 1$ links. Prim's algorithm, growing one tree from point 0, also works.",
    "Parallel example: to lay the least cable connecting five villages, keep choosing the shortest possible cable that joins two villages not already connected, ignoring cables that would close a loop."
  ],
